    "result_text": "All 52 tests pass, including the new `Cp38Tests`. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain email blocklist for `POST /api/owners`, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (a per-rule step + checked escalation + handler, wired in YAML \u2014 not `@ControllerAdvice`).\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/function/owner/RejectDisposableEmailDomain.java` \u2014 the pipeline step (a `Validate`-style guard reading the already-normalized `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`).\n- `rest/escalation/DisposableEmailDomainException.java` \u2014 checked exception thrown by the step.\n- `rest/escalation/DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `400` with `{\"errors\":[\"email\"]}`, mirroring the existing `InvalidEmailExceptionHandler`.\n- `officefloor/escalation/\u2026DisposableEmailDomainException.yml` \u2014 maps the exception to its handler.\n\n**Edited files:**\n- `OwnerEmails.java` \u2014 added a shared `rejectDisposableDomain(...)` helper holding the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`); absent emails pass through, present ones are matched exactly against the lower-cased domain.\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted an `emailBlocklist` step immediately after email normalization (so the value is already lower-cased) and before the rest of the pipeline.\n\nThe check sits after `NormalizeOwnerEmail`, so a syntactically-invalid email still returns 400 via the existing rule, and a valid-but-disposable domain now returns 400 via the new one. Optional/absent emails are unaffected. Full suite: **52 passed, 0 failures**.",
